 61CU2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61CU c  2001Ny01: Target of {+58}Ni evaporated on to carbon foil of            
 61CU2c  |?40 |mg/cm{+2}, was bombarded with 25-MeV |a particles from the Niels 
 61CU3c  Bohr Institute Tandem Accelerator. Measured angular distributions      
 61CU4c  protons from the (|a,p) reaction were momentum analyzed in multigap    
 61CU5c  spectrometer and registered with photographic emulsions. Spectra were  
 61CU6c  recorded at angles ranging from 7.5|' to 77.5|' in steps of 5|', and   
 61CU7c  energy resolution is |?25 keV. The emulsions were manually scanned in  
 61CU8c  1/2 mm strips. Spin and parity assignments made from comparison of     
 61CU9c  the experimental angular distributions of the emerging protons with    
 61CUAc  theoretical angular distributions calculated with the DWUCK-4 code     
 61CUBc  using a cluster form factor.                                           
 61CU c  1972Bu17: E|a=19.3 MeV. Semi, FWHM=150-200 keV. Enriched target.       
 61CU2c  Measured |s(|q), |q(c.m.)=10|'-130|'. A total of eight groups are      
 61CU3c  in the spectral figure 1, four of which (0, 470, 970 and 2700) were    
 61CU4c  analyzed for |s(|q) data                                               
 61CU c  1971Ho21: E|a=12.5 MeV. Magnetic spectrograph, FWHM=12 keV. |q(lab)=   
 61CU2c  90|' and 154|'. Levels up to 3978 keV.                                 
 61CU c  Others: 1965Le05, 1973Ma38.                                            
 61CU cL E$From 2001Ny01, except as noted. The uncertainties in 2001Ny01        
 61CU2cL are stated as |?2 keV for strongest groups and |?5 keV  for the        
 61CU3cL weakest groups. The evaluators assign these as follows: 2 keV for      
 61CU4cL d|s/d|W>50 |mb/sr and 5 keV for weaker peaks                           
 61CU cL J$ From |s(|q) data and comparisons with DWBA calculations (2001Ny01)  
 61CU cL E(B)$ The |s(|q) distribution shown in 1972Bu17 but no conclusions     
 61CU2cL about L-transfers have been drawn.                                     
 61CU cL E(A)$ From 1971Ho21, not reported in 2001Ny01.                         
 61CU cL E(D)$A doublet (from |g-ray data, see {+58}Ni(|a,p|g)).                
 61CU cL E(C)$ Probably the same as 3802 {I7} in 1971Ho21.                      
 61CU cL E(E)$ E(level) not reported in 1971Ho21.                               
 61CU cL E(F)$ Also reported in 1972Bu17. 2001Ny01 do not report this level,    
 61CU2cL however, in their spectral figure 2, a weak peak near this energy      
 61CU3cL is present.                                                            
 61CU cL S$The absolute cross sections were obtained by measuring the           
 61CU2cL (|a,p)-yield relative to elastic scattering at forward angles and      
 61CU3cL normalizing to optical model predictions, d|s/d|W (|mb/sr) measured    
 61CU4cL at 12.5 |' angle with the uncertainties above 20%.                     
